 "title": "A band inserted while the network runs keeps only the knots it has not reached",
 "subject": "Networks of rings joined by shared contacts, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law",
 "conclusion": "When the band law adds a band while the network runs, every ring whose influence has not reached the cut keeps all its knots across time and the new band is always bound, but most knots of the rings it has reached lapse. So persistent growth must come between runs, and under continual growth only the newest band stays bound.",
